  "manifestHash": "sha256:ef15e6448f7a73d258b83f743311907ccf6cd3161d65a29177d3518fb121f9d2",
  "model": {
    "description": "Partial source reconstruction of Level-0 definitions and scoped physical, optical, retinal, visual and neural records. Formal specifications, computational models, experimental preparations, reported observations and conditional interpretations have distinct meanings and evidence. Reviewed studies retain their own systems, selections, observables, uncertainty limits and unresolved contradictions. Physical records distinguish quantum-field definitions, scattering and decay measurements, Bell tests, vacuum quantities, QED and QCD running, lattice spectra and charge searches. Calibrated masses, detector unloading times, storage-loss rates and intrinsic-lifetime interpretations are separate quantities. Neutron survival studies retain production years, diagnostic controls, shared data and non-decay-loss corrections. Four-flavor QCD+QED mass splittings retain physical-point inputs, finite-volume prescriptions, convention-dependent components and the additional experimental input to a calibrated ratio. Capture-based neutron-mass inference distinguishes campaign angles, crystal calibration, nuclear recoil, unit conversions, adopted isotope masses and recalibration of shared data. Penning-trap inputs distinguish charge-normalized frequency ratios, voltage controls, neutral-atom corrections and correlated mass fits. LIONTRAP separates original acquisition, experimental reanalysis, shared-data controls and conditional electrode-geometry predictions. Proton-decay searches separate selected channel counts, nuclear and detector response, shared exposure, conditional partial-lifetime bounds and printed arithmetic. Magnetic-moment records distinguish electron and proton spin/cyclotron inference from neutron/mercury precession and its external absolute scale. Electron resonance fits, cavity calibration and radiative interpretations retain separate inputs and limits. Shared campaigns, source-specific correction conventions and uncertainty aggregation remain explicit. Cross-domain construction, universal carrier minima, downward causal rules and a derivation of quantum theory from Level 0 remain unestablished. No whole-graph scientific validation is claimed. Light-flavor families retain approximate representation conventions, a conditional historical Omega event and a response-corrected meson transition ratio; these do not establish real-time family formation. Perturbative amplitude and state-boundary conventions are separate from a synthetic kinematic check and from measured particle populations. No universal downward confinement mechanism is admitted. Free-field time evolution, historical electroweak mass relations and reactor-neutrino phase conventions retain specified models. Collider candidates and reactor signals are separated from response, backgrounds and fitted inferences; finite algebra does not reproduce those experiments. Solar active-flavor decomposition, atmospheric angular distributions and Higgs tau-pair evidence retain their original acquisitions and conditional fits. Matter evolution and coupling-rate definitions state their approximation boundaries; reused samples and post-fit displays are not independent experiments. Accelerator tau appearance and historical W/Z observations preserve selected candidates, adopted detector response and conditional original inferences. The single-doublet Higgs background and charged-fermion coupling are formal definitions with supplied parameters, distinct from a measured mass hierarchy or a universal stability mechanism.",
    "id": "causal-emergence",
    "name": "Causal Emergence — Canonical Reconstruction",
    "status": "research-reconstruction-partial",
    "version": "2026.10.02.9"
  },
